# The toolchain the Aether port is built and tested against. Pins are what
# was last verified, not "latest"; bump one in the commit that needs it (or
# that re-verified the port against it), as the other Aether repos do.
#
# Install both in one step (aeb's get.sh, pinned):
#   curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aether-lang-dev/aeb/main/get.sh \
#     | AE_PIN=$AE_PIN AEB_REF=$AEB_REF sh
#
# 0.909.0 (2026-11-12): the first pin. contrib.quickjs (quickjs-ng 0.17.0)
# is the engine; std.worker's run_detached gives a tool call its thread,
# std.sync its completion flag, std.os's spawn_proc_to a bash process group.
# Verified: aeb .tests.ae (20 suites, 156 tests, workspace.sh, check_layers.sh)
# on macOS arm64, ae-x64 (Ubuntu 22.04, kernel 5.15: no Landlock ABI 2, bash
# runs unsandboxed there as upstream) and cachyos (kernel 7.3: Landlock holds).
# Session + provider slice (2026-11-12), same pins: aeb .tests.ae green (35 suites)
# on macOS arm64, ae-x64 and cachyos; ae/tests/upstream-e2e.sh gives the same
# results on all three, except test_sandbox's workspace cases on ae-x64
# (kernel 5.15, no Landlock ABI 2: bash runs unsandboxed there, as upstream).
# 0.912.0 (2026-11-13): `import std.os hiding (...)` (0.911.0, aether #3653)
# makes "only tools/process, tools/jail and tui/open's launch start a program"
# a compile error (E0304) instead of a check_layers grep; the 0.910.0 fixes
# (aether #3655: a returned local optional owning a string, a local read once
# in a loop) let ae/term's surface loops store one blank again. std.posix.regex
# (#3654, 0.912.0) is not used. Verified: aeb .tests.ae, tools/tui_tests.sh and
# ae/tests/upstream-e2e.sh on macOS arm64, ae-x64 and cachyos.
# 0.914.0 (2026-11-14): aether #3694 fixes six asks and more (push of a call result,
# qualified slice locals, basename collision on qualified types, ptr as string,
# ipc SIGPIPE, run_stdio stderr_to/cwd, `ae run` exit on a failing spec); their
# stand-ins are removed in the same commit.
# 0.915.0 (2026-11-14): std.fs's stat (inode, mode, ns mtime), flock, O_EXCL,
# fd ops and positional writes, std.os.environ and signal_watch, std.io.set_echo
# replace naeb.sysgap, which is deleted.
# 0.916.0 (2026-11-14): contrib.quickjs gains eval_async, a host deadline with
# cancel and stop cells, promise_state/promise_result and a to_string that
# returns (string, error); quickjs-ng 0.18.0. naeb.qjsgap is deleted.
# 0.923.0 (2026-11-18): fs.unlink and fs.create_dir_with_mode return
# (ok, kind, msg), and std.fs has KIND_READ_ONLY_FS, KIND_BUSY and
# KIND_FILE_TOO_BIG (aether #3728); /undo's stat guess and fserr's POSIX errno
# numbers are gone. Verified: aeb .tests.ae 89/89 on macOS arm64 with the
# installed release.
# 0.931.0 (2026-11-20): a tracking-only bump, no new primitive needed and no
# source change. Verified: aeb .tests.ae on macOS arm64 (88 of 89; the red-team
# script's sockets need a checkout path under about 70 characters, and it passed
# 200 checks from a short path) and on ae-x64 (88 of 89 the same way; passed from
# a short path; ae/tests/llm_test.ae failed once under heavy load and passes alone).
# No provider traffic: mocks and fixtures only.
# 0.933.0 (2026-11-21): a tracking-only bump, no new primitive needed and no source
# change. Verified: aeb .tests.ae 89 of 89 on macOS arm64 from a short checkout
# path (34 characters), mocks and fixtures only, no provider traffic.
# 0.935.0 (2026-11-22): a tracking-only bump, no new primitive needed and no source
# change. Verified: aeb .tests.ae 88 of 89 on ae-x64 (Ubuntu 22.04 x86_64, aeb v0.349 as
# the runner, a 12-character checkout path), the one failure being ae/tests/redteam/run.sh,
# which passes alone from the same path (200 checks, 0 failures); the generated C of all 94
# programs is the same on 0.934.0 and 0.935.0. Mocks and fixtures only, no provider traffic.
# 0.936.0 (2026-11-22): a tracking-only bump, no new primitive needed and no source
# change. Verified: aeb .tests.ae 88 of 89 on ae-x64 (Ubuntu 22.04 x86_64, aeb main as
# the runner, a 60-character checkout path), the one failure being ae/tests/redteam/run.sh,
# which fails there because the egress proxy's socket path is too long for that checkout
# path and passes alone from a 6-character path (0 holes). Mocks and fixtures only, no provider traffic.
# 0.939.0 (2026-11-23): a tracking-only bump, no new primitive needed and no source
# change. 0.939.0 removes std.http.client's process-wide connection pool (aether #3851);
# naeb never configured it, and its requests (provider streams, MCP, web fetch and search,
# model listing, Maven) each open a connection and close it after the response, as they
# now do by default. No Step shares a connection: a stream may be abandoned on cancel or a
# timeout, which a reused connection must not survive. Verified: aeb .tests.ae minus its
# redteam/run.sh line on cachyos (Arch, a 12-character checkout path, a heavily loaded host):
# 85 of 89, the failures being ae/tests/tui_app_test.ae and tui_markdown_test.ae, which exit 0
# when their built binaries are run alone (the three bash tests passed); check_tests_vs_main.py
# clean; upstream-e2e.sh 28 of 30 (test_effort in its Codex half, test_session at its version
# assertion, both by policy). aeb .build.ae and naeb --version on macOS arm64. The fence,
# egress and sub-agent code are untouched, so the red-team suite was not run. Mocks and fixtures
# only, no provider traffic.
# 0.941.0 (2026-11-24): a tracking-only bump, no new primitive needed and no source
# change. 0.940.0 and 0.941.0 change the HTTP client's retry (only idempotent requests
# are retried after a failed read) and its error wording ("request timed out before the
# response arrived", "connection reset by the peer before the response arrived"); naeb's
# mock-driven tests and upstream's e2e suite match neither. Verified: aeb .tests.ae minus
# its redteam/run.sh line on cachyos (Arch, a 40-character checkout path): 89 of 89 PASS;
# upstream-e2e.sh 28 of 30 (test_effort in its Codex half, test_session at its version
# assertion, both by policy, as on 0.939.0). The fence, egress and sub-agent code are
# untouched, so the red-team suite was not run. Mocks and fixtures only, no provider traffic.
# 0.944.0 (2026-11-25): a tracking-only bump, no new primitive needed and no source
# change. 0.942.0-0.944.0 are performance only (runtime actor batching, inline std.math
# scalars, inline slice-view release). Verified on cachyos with aeb v0.349: aeb .tests.ae
# 88 of 90 (the two failures: ae/tests/agent_test.ae, a flaky ordering case that fails about
# 30 percent of runs on 0.941.0 and 0.944.0 alike on this loaded host, and the redteam
# line when the checkout path is too long for a unix socket; at a 10-character path under
# $HOME the redteam suite reports 0 holes, 216 ok, once refusal_records.py's own call was
# fixed). upstream-e2e.sh 28 of 30 (test_effort, test_session, both by policy, as before).
# Mocks and fixtures only, no provider traffic.
AE_PIN=0.944.0

